  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "George Adamski, a man who said in the 1950s that he had met friendly visitors from Venus, was in fact contacted by Nazis posing as Venusians, according to the writer Desmond Leslie, who co-wrote the book Flying Saucers Have Landed with him. The philosopher Jason Jorjani relays this second-hand, saying Leslie's daughter told him that \"her father said always said that it was Nazis who contacted Adamsky.\" If true, it would mean one of the best-known alien contact stories was a human deception."
